$\begin{aligned}
& P=P_1+P_2=-10 \\
& f=\frac{1}{P} \Rightarrow-0.1 \mathrm{~m} \Rightarrow-10 \mathrm{~cm}
\end{aligned}$

Bylens formula

$$

\begin{array}{l}

\frac{1}{v}-\frac{1}{u}=\frac{1}{f} \\

\frac{1}{v}-\frac{1}{(-20)}=\frac{10}{3} \\

\frac{1}{v}=\frac{10}{3}-\frac{1}{20} \\

\frac{1}{v}=\frac{197}{60} ; \quad v=\frac{60}{197}

\end{array}

$$

Magnification of lens (m) is given by

$$

\mathrm{m}=\left(\frac{\mathrm{v}}{\mathrm{u}}\right)=\frac{\left(\frac{60}{197}\right)}{20}

$$

velocity of image wrt. to lens is given by

$$

\mathrm{v}_{\mathrm{J} / \mathrm{L}}=\mathrm{m}^{2} \mathrm{v}_{\mathrm{O} / \mathrm{L}}

$$

direction of velocity of image is same as that of object

$$

\begin{array}{l}

\mathrm{v}_{\mathrm{O} / \mathrm{L}}=5 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s} \\

\mathrm{v}_{\mathrm{I} / \mathrm{L}}=\left(\frac{60 \times 1}{197 \times 20}\right)^{2}

\end{array}

$$

$=1.16 \times 10^{-3} \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}$ towards the lens

$$
\frac{1}{v}-\frac{1}{u}=\frac{1}{f}=\text { constant }
$$

For dispersion without deviation,
$\begin{aligned}
& \left(\mu_1-1\right) A_1=\left(\mu_2-1\right) A_2 \\
& \Rightarrow \quad(1.54-1) 4^{\circ}=(1.72-1) A_2 \\
& \text { Or } A_2=\frac{0.54}{0.72} \times 4=3^{\circ}
\end{aligned}$

Normal to the plane is $z$-axis
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \cos \theta_1=\frac{A_z}{A}=\frac{10}{20}=\frac{1}{2}, \theta_1=60 \\
& \mu_1 \sin \theta_1=\mu_2 \sin \theta_2 \Rightarrow \sqrt{2} \times \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}=\sqrt{3} \sin \theta_2 \Rightarrow \theta_2=45^{\circ}
\end{aligned}
$$
